regarding the state's finances.

And for context for you all, relative to
before I start in on the details of the debt
report, I wanted to share with you my
perspective -- from a macro perspective, the
favorable climate that we have been operating in.

What I mean by that is two fundamental
factors: One is a favorable interest rate
environment, and the second is a very strong
economy .

So the two things that are most important to
us from a credit perspective have been working in
our favor.

And what I would say, as an overlay of that,
more specifically with respect to municipal market
conditions, we have dollars flowing into the space
to be invested; and we have interest rates that
are very low. So the combination of those factors
has led to very strong demand for municipal bonds
and has kept us in the game on our ability to be
able to reduce our long-term costs through
refinancings.

Specifically on the debt report, I would say
that it is a continuation, but I mean that in a

very positive way because we have the wind at our

