Well, I'm happy to report, at the end of 2019
the actual number is 4.65 percent. So we're south
of our target ratio, again because of the
combination of limited debt issuance, reduced debt
service cost, and growing revenues.

So we're well positioned with debt capacity
available to fund critical infrastructure needs.
And just so I don't get accused of giving only good
news, a dose of sobriety, two things that I see
that I would like to make note of and are noted in
the report, really messaging the Legislature; and
that is, vulnerabilities with respect to our
rating.

What are those? One, maintaining adequate
reserves; and two, adequately funding the pension.
So those are the two things that I see that --
where the state is vulnerable in terms of over
the long term maintaining our stellar credit
ratings.

