With respect to pension funding and the
liability, we've got an estimated $25 billion in
the unfunded liability, $25 billion. That's more
debt -- that's more than the debt that we have
outstanding for all -- in the aggregate of
everything that we borrowed to fund bricks and
sticks and infrastructure throughout the state.

The state share of that -- because it's a
multi-employer plan, there are some four to five
hundred participants in the plan, the state
employees are just one element of that. Our share
of that, state share of that, 20 percent.

And with respect to vulnerabilities and
progress to be made, and we've been very direct and
vocal about this with respect to the estimating
conference, it's getting the assumptions right.
It's getting the numbers right that we use to
calculate how much is necessary to adequately fund
the pension.

And while we've made progress on that front,

over the last five years, we've moved the --

