15

probably the single factor that the rating agencies
are focused on two things: What is your return
assumption? What do you expect to earn on the
investment returns of the Florida Retirement
System?

And the second is: What kind of actuarial
methodologies are using to calculate the amount
necessary to adequately fund the pension?

And while we've made progress, reducing that
return assumption from 7.75 percent to 7.4 percent
over the last five years, and importantly, with
support from the Governor's office doubling down on
that -- and what I mean by that is making a
20-basis point move in the return assumption from
7.4 percent to 7.2 percent.

So we are moving in the right direction, but
we still have more work to be done in that space.
And a plan would be -- a legislatively articulated
plan on how to get from Point A to Point B, i.e. to
a reasonable investment return, would be an
extraordinarily important signal to send to the
rating agencies that we understand the magnitude of
the challenges and we're working to address those.

CFO PATRONIS: Thanks.

GOVERNOR DESANTIS: Great. Thank you.

